  {"production":"parse_with_clause","construct":"with","file":"core/src/parser/grammar/cte.rs","doc":"Parse WITH clause including optional RECURSIVE keyword.\n\nGrammar contract:\n```text\nWITH [RECURSIVE] name[(cols)] AS ( <body> ) [, ...] <main-query>\n```\n\nAll CTE bodies are parsed strictly as QAIL DSL (no raw-SQL fallback).\n\nWhen RECURSIVE is present, each CTE body must additionally:\n- Must contain exactly one top-level `UNION ALL`\n- Both halves must parse as valid QAIL (no raw-SQL fallback)\n- Base must NOT reference the CTE name, recursive part MUST reference it","example":null,"keywords":["recursive","with"],"calls":["parse_cte_definition"]},
  {"production":"parse_cte_definition","construct":"cte_definition","file":"core/src/parser/grammar/cte.rs","doc":"Parse a single CTE definition: name [(columns)] AS (subquery)","example":null,"keywords":["as"],"calls":["parse_identifier","parse_qail_strict","parse_recursive_cte_strict"]},
  {"production":"parse_recursive_cte_strict","construct":"recursive_cte_strict","file":"core/src/parser/grammar/cte.rs","doc":"Strict recursive CTE parser pipeline (steps 2-6 from QA spec).\n\n1. Split body on top-level `UNION ALL`\n2. Parse both halves strictly (no raw-SQL fallback)\n3. Validate: base must NOT reference CTE name, recursive MUST reference it\n4. Build CTEDef structurally with both base_query and recursive_query","example":null,"keywords":[],"calls":["parse_qail_strict"]},
